shutters:
’Gainst angels: henceforth it is night with me,
And so, henceforth, I put the shutters up;
Auroras must not come to spoil my dark.’

shuffle:
Dark figures start for work;
I watch them sadly shuffle on,
’Tis dawn, dawn in New York.

shuffling:
I cut and shuffle; shuffle, cut, again;
But all my cutting, shuffling, proves in vain:
Vain hope, vain forethought too;

shure:
Be quick as ye kin fur he's right at the dure;
Come in, master Tim, fur ye're welcome I'm shure.
We were talkin' o' ye jest a minute before.

shun:
The farthest boundaries of thought,
And shun no end which these have brought;
Then die in satisfaction, knowing

shun'd:
Let sin, that baneful evil to the soul,
By you be shun'd, nor once remit your guard;
Suppress the deadly serpent in its egg.

shuns:
The softly stealing echo comes again
From crowds of men whom, wearily, he shuns;
And many see you there--so his thought runs--
